it/components/CaSlipModal.js)):**\n  - Click **\"📑 CA Audit Slip\"** at any time to print or download an A4 audit certificate reflecting your current inputs.\n- **\"✍️ Enter Bill Manually\" Dashboard Action ([`DashboardHero.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/DashboardHero.js)):**\n  - Shopkeepers can audit physical counter parchas from scratch without needing to upload a file.\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Try It Live\n\n1. Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) in your browser.\n2. Click **Sample 2: Math Error** (Modern Electrical Supplies) to see the ₹1,000 overcharge.\n3. In the line items table, change the **LED Bulb Billed Amount** from `₹2,900` to `₹1,900`, or click **\"🪄 Auto-Fix Bill Math\"**—watch the discrepancy drop to ₹0 and the red banner flip to green verified in real time!\n4. Move the **Digital Receipts Ratio slider** in the Tax Insights card to watch your **Deemed Net Profit** and **Estimated Tax** recalculate instantly.\n5. Click **\"📲 Share on WhatsApp\"** to test the live dispute note generator."}
{"step_index":145,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:11:38Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nYou are an invoice parsing engine for AUDIT IT.\n\nTASK:\n1. Examine the provided document or image.\n2. First, determine if this is a genuine business invoice, cash memo, purchase bill, or tax receipt.\n3. IF IT IS NOT an invoice (e.g. it is a person's photo, landscape, screenshot of a chat, unrelated document, or random text):\n   - Set `is_valid_bill` to false.\n   - Set `rejection_reason` explaining why (e.g. \"Uploaded image is not a financial bill or invoice\").\n   - Leave all financial fields null or empty.\n4. IF IT IS AN INVOICE:\n   - Set `is_valid_bill` to true.\n   - Extract the fields as accurately as possible.\n   - NEVER make up or hallucinate missing data. If a field (like GSTIN or invoice number) is not present or unreadable, set it to null and append it to `unreadable_fields`.\n\nmake the app strictly calculate and analyse the given inputs with precision \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-02T19:41:38+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
