{"step_index":218,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:16:35Z","input_tokens":2843,"cache_read_tokens":179067,"output_tokens":1765,"content":"### Document Gatekeeper & Precision Engine Implemented\n\nWe have integrated the **Invoice Validation Gatekeeper** and **Precision Calculation Engine** into the AUDIT IT parsing pipeline ([`utils/aiExtractor.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js) and [`utils/auditEngine.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/auditEngine.js)).\n\n---\n\n### 🛡️ 1. Gatekeeper Validation & Parsing Pipeline\n\nThe extraction prompt and parser enforce the strict 2-step verification rule:\n\n```text\nYou are an invoice parsing engine for AUDIT IT.\n\nTASK:\n1. Examine the provided document or image.\n2. First, determine if this is a genuine business invoice, cash memo, purchase bill, or tax receipt.\n3. IF IT IS NOT an invoice (e.g. it is a person's photo, landscape, screenshot of a chat, unrelated document, or random text):\n   - Set is_valid_bill to false.\n   - Set rejection_reason explaining why (e.g. \"Uploaded image is not a financial bill or invoice\").\n   - Leave all financial fields null or empty.\n4. IF IT IS AN INVOICE:\n   - Set is_valid_bill to true.\n   - Extract the fields as accurately as possible.\n   - NEVER make up or hallucinate missing data. If a field (like GSTIN or invoice number) is not present or unreadable, set it to null and append it to unreadable_fields.\n   - Extract exact declared amounts; DO NOT fix math mistakes in the extraction.\n```\n\n#### JSON Output Schema:\n```json\n{\n  \"is_valid_bill\": true,\n  \"rejection_reason\": null,\n  \"unreadable_fields\": [],\n  \"vendor_name\": \"Modern Electrical Supplies Pvt Ltd\",\n  \"vendor_address\": \"Plot 88, Lamington Road, Mumbai - 400007\",\n  \"gstin\": \"27AABCM8291Q1Z8\",\n  \"invoice_no\": \"MES/MUM/2026/894\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-10-30\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"2.5 sq mm Copper Wire Coil (90m)\",\n      \"hsn\": \"8544\",\n      \"qty\": 10,\n      \"rate\": 1200.00,\n      \"amount\": 12000.00,\n      \"is_blurry\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"subtotal\": 17150.00,\n  \"cgst\": 1543.50,\n  \"sgst\": 1543.50,\n  \"igst\": 0.00,\n  \"total_declared\"\n<truncated 631 bytes>\n callout explaining that no financial figures will be generated for invalid media.\n  - Direct action button: **\"← Upload a Genuine Bill\"**.\n\n---\n\n### 🔢 3. Strict Precision Calculations ([`utils/auditEngine.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/auditEngine.js))\n\nAll calculations run with float precision and epsilon correction (`round2`):\n\n1. **Line-Item Level Check:**\n   $$\\text{calculated\\_amount} = \\text{round2}(\\text{qty} \\times \\text{rate})$$\n   $$\\text{diff} = \\text{declared\\_amount} - \\text{calculated\\_amount}$$\n   - Any variance exceeding 50 paise ($\\pm ₹0.50$) triggers a line-level calculation error with the exact discrepancy amount.\n2. **Deterministic Subtotal & GST Total:**\n   $$\\text{sum\\_items} = \\sum (\\text{qty} \\times \\text{rate})$$\n   $$\\text{total\\_tax} = \\text{cgst} + \\text{sgst} + \\text{igst}$$\n   $$\\text{calculated\\_total} = \\text{sum\\_items} + \\text{total\\_tax}$$\n3. **Declared Grand Total Discrepancy:**\n   $$\\text{totalDiff} = \\text{total\\_declared} - \\text{calculated\\_total}$$\n   - If $|\\text{totalDiff}| > ₹1.00$, the engine flags a calculation discrepancy (overcharge or undercharge).\n4. **Missing & Unreadable Fields:**\n   - Any field flagged in `unreadable_fields` is logged with an audit warning: *\"Never hallucinated: field missing on paper bill. User verification required.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Test the Rejection & Precision Engine\n\nIn the app at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000):\n1. **Test Rejection:** Click **\"Sample 4: Non-Invoice Photo\"** on the right column of the dashboard. Observe how the gatekeeper rejects the image, leaves all financial totals empty, and provides the clear rejection reason.\n2. **Test Precision Audit:** Click **\"Sample 2: Math Error\"** to see precision item checking catch the exact ₹1,000 line item error and ₹1,180 total overcharge.\n3. **Upload Real Photos:** Try dropping or uploading any photo—valid invoices parse into live precision audits, while selfies or random screenshots trigger the rejection gatekeeper.","thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
