{"step_index":220,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:20:36Z","input_tokens":2592,"cache_read_tokens":181193,"output_tokens":1139,"thinking":"The problem is mismatched data between the uploaded document and the displayed digitized output. The current display shows unrelated, hardcoded items instead of reflecting the uploaded invoice data. The goal is to correct this mismatch without modifying the core features.\n\n\nThe mismatch stems from the code's fallback mechanism. When an API key is missing or invalid, the system defaults to hardcoded items in `simulateLocalExtraction`, which bypasses real data extraction and creates the discrepancy. This function is returning the static items when the Gemini API is unavailable. The issue needs to be corrected by ensuring accurate extraction or a proper error handling in the fallback scenario.\n\n\nReal-time OCR extraction is feasible using Tesseract.js directly in the browser, 